    before: []  # 7b90
    duplicate_of: []  # 7b90
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 7b90
    pr_ref:  # 7b90
    description: "## Background\n\nThe CI Interaction Policy in AGENTS.md says:\n\n> - **NEVER** call the Forgejo API directly outside of approved scripts.\n> - **Approved scripts** (exhaustive list): `auto-pr`, `merge-pr`, `ci-debug`, `contribute`. All CI/API interaction MUST go through these.\n\nThis is a sound rule — it centralizes all forge interactions in a small,\nauditable set of files (which are also governance files), prevents agents\nfrom writing ad-hoc curl/poll loops, and keeps credential handling in one\nplace. It should not be relaxed.\n\nHowever, the rule has a coverage gap: there is currently no sanctioned\npath for **closing a PR without merging it**. None of the four approved\nscripts expose a `close <PR>` action:\n\n- `auto-pr` does call `api_patch '{\"state\": \"closed\"}'` internally at\n  scripts/auto-pr:774, but only as part of the hung-run retry loop —\n  it is not exposed as a standalone subcommand.\n- `merge-pr` only merges.\n- `ci-debug` is read-only.\n- `contribute` is for the external-contributor fork workflow.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nAgents periodically encounter PRs that should be closed without merging:\n\n1. **No-op PRs from tracker auto-sync.** See the sibling tracker item\n   for the empty-commit bug. Until that root cause is fixed, empty\n   tracker-sync PRs will appear occasionally and need manual closure.\n   PR https://codeberg.org/iterabloom/hypergumbo/pulls/2729 is the\n   triggering example.\n2. **Superseded feature PRs.** When an agent abandons a branch in\n   favor of a different approach, the old PR should be closed.\n3. **Diagnosed-as-wrong PRs.** When CI surfaces a fundamental problem\n   that means the PR should not land at all (rather than be fixed),\n   close-without-merge is the right action.\n\nIn all three cases, the agent today has to either:\n- Ask the human to close the PR via the web UI (this is what I had to\n  do for #2729), or\n- Violate the CI Interaction Policy by sourcing `lib/forgejo-api.sh`\n  inline and calling api_patch directly.\n\nNeither is good. The first is friction that scales with the number\nof stale PRs. The second normalizes policy violations.\n\n## Proposal\n\nAdd a `close` subcommand to `merge-pr` (the most natural home — the\nscript is already about transitioning a PR to a terminal state). The\ninterface should be minimal:\n\n    ./scripts/merge-pr close <PR_NUM> [--reason \"free-text reason\"]\n\nBehavior:\n1. Validate the PR number is open and not already merged\n   (refuse to \"close\" a merged PR).\n2. Optionally post a comment with the supplied reason before closing,\n   so the audit trail is preserved on the forge side.\n3. PATCH the PR to `{\"state\": \"closed\"}` via the existing `api_patch`\n   helper from `lib/forgejo-api.sh`.\n4. Print confirmation, exit 0 on success, non-zero on any failure.\n\nAlternative: add it to `auto-pr` instead, since that script already\ncontains the close-PR call site internally. Either is fine. `merge-pr`\nfeels slightly cleaner because `auto-pr` is conceptually about *creating*\nPRs and `merge-pr` is about *resolving* them.\n\n## Why this requires human approval (status: needs_human_review)\n\nBoth `merge-pr` and `auto-pr` are governance files per AGENTS.md:\n\n> **Governance Files:** Changes to ... `scripts/auto-pr`, `scripts/merge-pr`,\n> ... require human approval. Do NOT self-merge PRs touching these files.\n\nPer the governance approval workflow, the agent must NOT preemptively\ncreate a PR for this. Instead, this item is filed as `needs_human_review`,\nthe human reviews and approves the proposal here in the tracker discussion,\nand then implementation can proceed via `auto-pr` (which will produce a PR\nthat gets human-reviewed and merged, not self-merged).\n\n## Testing requirements\n\nTests must live in the same package as `merge-pr` (or `auto-pr`,\ndepending on which the human picks). Required:\n- Happy path: close an open PR → `{\"state\": \"closed\"}` PATCH is sent,\n  exit 0, output confirms closure.\n- Refusal: attempt to close a PR that is already merged → exit non-zero\n  with a clear error  # 7b90
      message, no PATCH sent.\n- Refusal: attempt to close a PR that is already closed → idempotent\n  no-op (or refuse — TBD by reviewer).\n- Network failure: curl returns non-zero / non-2xx → script exits\n  non-zero with diagnostic, does not silently swallow.\n- Comment posting (if implemented): when --reason is supplied, the\n  comment POST happens before the close PATCH, and a failure to post\n  the comment does not block the close (or does — TBD by reviewer).\n\n100% coverage required per AGENTS.md.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThis item is just about adding the close subcommand. Things that are\nNOT in scope here and should be separate items if pursued:\n\n- Automatic stale-PR detection / cleanup. (Different problem; this\n  item is just about the imperative tool.)\n- Bulk close operations. (`merge-pr close 2729 2730 2731` could be\n  added later if there's demand.)\n- Reopening closed PRs. (Different action; can be added separately.)\n\n## Priority justification\n\nP4 (lowest). The current friction is real but small — the agent can\njust ask the human to click a button on the forge UI. The cost of NOT\nhaving this tool is one extra round-trip per stale PR encountered,\nwhich is rare. Worth doing eventually for consistency, but nothing\nblocks on it."  # 7b90
    fields: {}  # 7b90
